IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bnra-types`

-- Business Names Registration Act 2014, Part 3 (ss 32 to 45): inspection, information,
-- offences and penalties, composition, records, enforcement, bodies corporate, service,
-- regulations and transitional provisions.
-- Source: source/BNRA2014.txt lines 1459 to 2014.  The Act has no Schedules.

§ `Part 3 -- Miscellaneous`

§§ `32. Inspection`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 32(1)"
GIVEN i IS AN `Inspection Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is validly authorised as an inspector` IF
        i's `the Registrar has authorised the person in writing to be an inspector`
    AND i's `the person authorised is an employee of the Authority or a public officer`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 32(2)"
GIVEN i IS AN `Inspection Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar or an inspector may enter the premises` IF
    i's `the Registrar or inspector has reason to believe a person is carrying on business at the premises`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 32(3)"
GIVEN i IS AN `Inspection Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar or inspector has complied with section 32(3)` IF
        i's `the Registrar or inspector declared his or her office`
    AND i's `the Registrar or inspector produced his or her written authority to the person affected`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 32(4) and (5)"
GIVEN i IS AN `Inspection Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty of an offence under section 32(4)` IF
        i's `the person fails to comply with a request made by, or resists or obstructs, the Registrar or an inspector in the performance of his or her duties`
    AND `the Registrar or inspector has complied with section 32(3)` i

§§ `33. Power of Registrar to obtain further information`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 33(1)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Information Request Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may require the person to answer in writing or summon the person to answer orally` IF
    r's `the person is a person carrying on business, an employee of that person, a person apparently employed at that person's place of business, or a person apparently managing that person's business`

-- 33(2): the Registrar may further require a declaration or particulars: a power with no
-- condition, inert.  Failing to comply without lawful excuse is an offence under
-- s 35(1)(b) (`the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(1)(b)`).

§§ `34. Restriction on undischarged bankrupt carrying on business`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 34(3)"
GIVEN b IS A `Bankrupt Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the General Division of the High Court may give permission` IF
    b's `notice of intention to apply to the General Division of the High Court was served on the Official Assignee and the Official Assignee was heard`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 34(1)"
GIVEN b IS A `Bankrupt Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the undischarged bankrupt is guilty of an offence under section 34(1)` IF
        b's `the person is an undischarged bankrupt, adjudicated by a Singapore court or a foreign court having jurisdiction in bankruptcy`
    AND (   b's `the person is required to be registered and carries on business in Singapore`
         OR b's `the person directly or indirectly takes part in or is concerned in the management of a business carried on by a person required to be registered`)
    AND NOT b's `the General Division of the High Court has given permission`
    AND NOT b's `the Official Assignee has given written permission`

-- 34(2): on an application the court or Official Assignee may refuse or approve on
-- conditions: a discretion with no condition of its own, inert.

§§ `35. Offences and penalties`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 35(1)(a) and (2)"
GIVEN o IS AN `Offence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(1)(a)` IF
        o's `the person is required to be registered`
    AND NOT o's `the person is not required to be registered in respect of the business name under section 4`
    AND (   o's `the person carries on business in Singapore without being registered`
         OR o's `the person carries on business in Singapore under a business name different from the registered business name`
         OR o's `the person carries on business under a business name after the registration in respect of it has been cancelled`
         OR o's `the person carries on business under a business name after the registration in respect of it has ceased`)

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 35(1)(b)"
GIVEN o IS AN `Offence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(1)(b)` IF
    o's `the person, without lawful excuse, fails to comply with a summons or requisition of the Registrar under section 33`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 35(1)(c)"
GIVEN o IS AN `Offence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(1)(c)` IF
        o's `the person makes a statement or provides information to the Registrar that is false in a material particular or by omission of a material particular`
    AND o's `the person knows or has reason to believe it is false`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 35(3)"
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with section 19(1) or 20(1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty of an offence under section 35(3)` IF
    `the person fails to comply with section 19(1) or 20(1) or (3)`

-- The maximum penalty for each offence provision in the Act.

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, ss 11(12), 22(3), 32(4), 34(1), 35(1), 35(3), 43(3), 45(5)(b)"
GIVEN p IS AN `Offence Provision`
GIVETH A `Penalty`
`the maximum penalty for the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `failing to appoint an authorised representative or to lodge a notice (section 11(12))` THEN Penalty OF 1_000, NOTHING
    WHEN `failing to notify cessation of business (section 22(3))` THEN Penalty OF 5_000, NOTHING
    WHEN `failing to comply with a request of, or obstructing, the Registrar or an inspector (section 32(4))` THEN Penalty OF 10_000, JUST 24
    WHEN `an undischarged bankrupt carrying on or managing business (section 34(1))` THEN Penalty OF 10_000, JUST 24
    WHEN `carrying on business unregistered, failing to comply with a summons, or a false statement (section 35(1))` THEN Penalty OF 10_000, JUST 24
    WHEN `failing to comply with section 19(1) or 20(1) or (3) (section 35(3))` THEN Penalty OF 5_000, JUST 12
    WHEN `contravening regulations that so provide (section 43(3))` THEN Penalty OF 5_000, JUST 12
    WHEN `failing to appoint an authorised representative after commencement (section 45(5)(b))` THEN Penalty OF 1_000, NOTHING

§§ `36. Evidence of carrying on business under business name`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 36(a) and (b)"
GIVEN d IS A `Display Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is presumed to be carrying on the business under that business name` IF
        d's `proof is given that a business name has been displayed in premises`
    AND d's `evidence is given from which the court may infer that the business name refers to a business carried on at the premises`
    AND NOT d's `there is proof to the contrary`

§§ `37. Composition of offences`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 37(1)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN c IS A `Composition Facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be collected in composition` MEANS
    IF c's `the maximum fine prescribed for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2 LESS THAN 5_000
    THEN c's `the maximum fine prescribed for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2
    ELSE 5_000

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 37(1)"
GIVEN c IS A `Composition Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for the sum proposed` IF
        c's `the offence is prescribed as a compoundable offence`
    AND c's `the sum proposed to be collected` AT MOST `the most that may be collected in composition` c

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 37(2)"
GIVEN c IS A `Composition Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no further proceedings are to be taken against the person in respect of the offence` IF
    c's `the sum has been paid`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 37(1) and s 43(2)(j)"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no regulations under section 43(2)(j) prescribing compoundable offences are encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "no regulations under section 43(2)(j) prescribing compoundable offences are encoded in this model"

§§ `38. Destruction or transfer of old records`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 38(a)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Old Record Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may destroy the document` IF
        r's `the document was filed, lodged, submitted or issued under this Act`
    AND r's `the document has been microfilmed or converted to electronic form`
    AND r's `the Registrar is of the opinion that it is no longer necessary or desirable to retain the document`
    AND r's `the National Library Board has authorised the destruction under section 17 of the National Library Board Act 1995`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 38(b)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Old Record Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may transfer the document to the National Archives of Singapore` IF
        r's `the document was filed, lodged, submitted or issued under this Act`
    AND r's `the document has been microfilmed or converted to electronic form`
    AND r's `the Registrar is of the opinion that it is no longer necessary or desirable to retain the document`

§§ `39. Enforcement of duty to make returns`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 39(1)(a)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Enforcement Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the non-compliance was not made good within 14 days after service of the notice` IF
        e's `the person failed to comply with a provision of this Act, or a provision of another written law requiring a return, account, notice or other document to be filed with the Registrar`
    AND e's `the Registrar served notice to comply`
    AND (CONSIDER e's `the date the person made good the non-compliance, if it has been made good`
         WHEN JUST made THEN made GREATER THAN e's `the date of service of the Registrar's notice to comply` PLUS 14
         WHEN NOTHING THEN e's `the date on which the court considers the Registrar's application` GREATER THAN e's `the date of service of the Registrar's notice to comply` PLUS 14)

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 39(1)(b)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Enforcement Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the request to amend or resubmit was not complied with within 14 days after service` IF
        e's `the Registrar requested the person to amend, complete and resubmit a document or to submit a fresh document`
    AND (CONSIDER e's `the date the person complied with that request, if the person has`
         WHEN JUST complied THEN complied GREATER THAN e's `the date of service of that request` PLUS 14
         WHEN NOTHING THEN e's `the date on which the court considers the Registrar's application` GREATER THAN e's `the date of service of that request` PLUS 14)

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 39(1)(c)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Enforcement Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person failed to take the steps the Registrar requested under section 27(7)` IF
        e's `the Registrar made a request under section 27(7) to take steps within a time to rectify an error or defect`
    AND e's `the person failed to take those steps within the time specified`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 39(1)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Enforcement Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make an order directing the relevant person to make good the failure` IF
        e's `the application is made by the Registrar`
    AND (CONSIDER e's `the court`
         WHEN `a District Court` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a Magistrate's Court` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `any other court` THEN FALSE)
    AND (   `the non-compliance was not made good within 14 days after service of the notice` e
         OR `the request to amend or resubmit was not complied with within 14 days after service` e
         OR `the person failed to take the steps the Registrar requested under section 27(7)` e)

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 39(4)"
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of Business Holder`
GIVETH A STRING
`the relevant person` MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an individual proprietor` THEN "that individual"
    WHEN `a firm` THEN "all or any of its partners"
    WHEN `a corporation` THEN "the corporation, any of its officers as defined in section 40(5), or both"
    WHEN `a person who carries on business wholly or mainly as nominee of or trustee for another person` THEN "the firstmentioned person, the nominee or trustee"

-- 39(2) (costs may be borne by a relevant person) and 39(3) (other penalties are not
-- limited): a power to order costs and a saving, inert.

§§ `40. Offences by bodies corporate, etc.`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 40(1) to (4)"
GIVEN b IS A `Body Offence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty of the offence as well as the body` IF
        b's `an offence under this Act committed by the body is proved`
    AND (   b's `the offence was committed with the person's consent or connivance`
         OR b's `the offence is attributable to neglect on the person's part`)
    AND (CONSIDER b's `kind of body`
         WHEN `a body corporate, including a limited liability partnership` THEN
             (CONSIDER b's `the person's role`
              WHEN `an officer of the body corporate` THEN TRUE
              WHEN `a member of a body corporate whose affairs are managed by its members, acting in connection with the member's functions of management` THEN TRUE
              OTHERWISE FALSE)
         WHEN `a firm` THEN
             (CONSIDER b's `the person's role`
              WHEN `a partner of the firm, including a person purporting to act as a partner` THEN TRUE
              OTHERWISE FALSE)
         WHEN `an unincorporated association other than a firm` THEN
             (CONSIDER b's `the person's role`
              WHEN `an officer of the unincorporated association or a member of its governing body` THEN TRUE
              OTHERWISE FALSE))

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 40(6)"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no regulations under section 40(6) modifying section 40 for bodies formed outside Singapore are encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "no regulations under section 40(6) modifying section 40 for bodies formed outside Singapore are encoded in this model"

-- 40(5) defines "body corporate", "officer" and "partner": these fix the roles listed in
-- `Role in Body`, inert.

§§ `41. Authority and its employees not liable`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 41"
GIVEN l IS A `Liability Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is not liable for the error or inaccuracy` IF
        l's `the person is the Authority, the Registrar or another officer or employee of the Authority`
    AND l's `there is an error or inaccuracy in the register, or in a certificate, certified extract, copy or other document made or issued under this Act`
    AND NOT l's `the error or inaccuracy was due to a lack of reasonable care and good faith on the part of the Registrar or another officer or employee of the Authority`

§§ `42. Service of documents, etc.`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of Recipient`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recipient is an individual` IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an individual` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a firm` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a corporation or an unincorporated association` THEN FALSE

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of Recipient`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recipient is a firm` IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an individual` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a firm` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a corporation or an unincorporated association` THEN FALSE

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of Recipient`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recipient is a corporation or an unincorporated association` IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an individual` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a firm` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a corporation or an unincorporated association` THEN TRUE

-- 42(1) lists the routes of service for each kind of recipient; 42(3) allows email only
-- with the person's prior written consent.

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 42(1)(a), (b) and (c), and (3)"
GIVEN r IS A `Service Route`
      k IS A `Kind of Recipient`
      `the person has given prior written consent to service by email` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the route of service is permitted` IF
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `delivering it to the individual personally` THEN
        `the recipient is an individual` k
    WHEN `leaving it with an adult apparently resident at the usual or last known address of the individual's residence` THEN
        `the recipient is an individual` k
    WHEN `sending it by ordinary or prepaid registered post to the usual or last known address of the individual's residence` THEN
        `the recipient is an individual` k
    WHEN `leaving it with an adult apparently resident or employed at, or posting it to, the individual's contact address` THEN
        `the recipient is an individual` k
    WHEN `leaving it with an adult apparently employed at, or posting it to, the usual or last known address of the individual's place of business` THEN
        `the recipient is an individual` k
    WHEN `affixing a copy in a conspicuous place at the individual's contact address or usual or last known address of residence or business` THEN
        `the recipient is an individual` k
    WHEN `delivering it to any one of the partners or the secretary or other like officer of the firm` THEN
        `the recipient is a firm` k
    WHEN `leaving it at, or posting it to, the principal or last known place of business of the firm in Singapore` THEN
        `the recipient is a firm` k
    WHEN `delivering it to the secretary or other like officer of the corporation or unincorporated association, or the manager of a limited liability partnership` THEN
        `the recipient is a corporation or an unincorporated association` k
    WHEN `leaving it at, or posting it to, the registered office or principal office of the corporation or unincorporated association in Singapore` THEN
        `the recipient is a corporation or an unincorporated association` k
    WHEN `sending it by fax to the fax number given to the Registrar` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sending it by email to the last email address given to the Registrar` THEN
        `the person has given prior written consent to service by email`

-- 42(2): when a document served by or for the Registrar or the Minister is deemed served.

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 42(2)(a) to (e)"
GIVEN m IS A `Service Method`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the date the document is deemed served` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `personal delivery` delivered THEN JUST delivered
    WHEN `ordinary post` ordinary returned THEN (IF returned THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (ordinary PLUS 1))
    WHEN `prepaid registered post` posted THEN JUST (posted PLUS 2)
    WHEN `fax` transmitted successful THEN (IF successful THEN JUST transmitted ELSE NOTHING)
    WHEN `email` retrievable THEN JUST retrievable

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 42(4)(a), (b) and (c)"
GIVEN s IS A `Summons Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the summons has been served` IF
        s's `the summons is delivered to the person`
     OR s's `the summons is delivered to an adult residing at the person's last known place of residence`
     OR s's `the summons is sent by prepaid registered post in a cover addressed to the person at the person's last known place of residence or business or an address the person provided`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 42(5)"
GIVEN s IS A `Summons Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `service of the summons by prepaid registered post is sufficiently proved` IF
    s's `the cover was properly addressed, stamped and posted by prepaid registered post`

§§ `43. Regulations`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 43(1) and (2)"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no regulations under section 43 are encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "no regulations under section 43 are encoded in this model"

-- 43(2)(a) to (k) list the matters regulations may cover, and 43(3) lets them create an
-- offence punishable by a fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12
-- months or both (the last is `the maximum penalty for the offence`).  The list is inert.

§§ `44. Saving for other written law`

-- 44: unless expressly provided, nothing in the Act limits or affects any other written law:
-- a rule of construction, inert.

§§ `45. Saving and transitional provisions`

-- 45(1): persons who were Registrar, Deputy Registrar or Assistant Registrar under the
-- repealed Act are treated as appointed under s 3(2) until their term ends: an allocation
-- of office, inert.  45(3): the Registrar is to transfer the old register: administrative,
-- inert.

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 45(2)"
GIVEN t IS A `Transitional Registration Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is treated as registered under section 8` IF
    t's `the person was registered or deemed registered under the repealed Act immediately before 3 January 2016`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 45(2)"
GIVEN t IS A `Transitional Registration Facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the date the treated registration expires` MEANS
    t's `the date the registration would have expired if this Act had not been enacted`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 45(4)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN l IS A `Local Manager Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the local manager is treated as the authorised representative from 3 January 2016` IF
        l's `the person (A) was registered as a local manager appointed by a person carrying on business (B) under regulations made under the repealed Act before 3 January 2016`
    AND NOT l's `A or B lodged a notice within 30 days after 3 January 2016 that A has not been appointed as B's authorised representative`
    AND NOT l's `A or B lodged a notice within 30 days after 3 January 2016 that A does not meet the criteria in section 11(2)`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 45(5)"
GIVEN r IS A `Transitional Residence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an authorised representative had to be appointed within 30 days after 3 January 2016` IF
        r's `the registrant is treated as registered under section 45(2)`
    AND r's `the individual proprietor, all the partners of the firm or all the officers of the foreign company reside outside Singapore on 3 January 2016`
    AND NOT r's `section 45(4) applies`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 45(5)"
`the last day for appointing an authorised representative under section 45(5)` MEANS YMD 2016 1 3 PLUS 30

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 45(5)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN r IS A `Transitional Residence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may cancel, and each is guilty of an offence, under section 45(5)` IF
        `an authorised representative had to be appointed within 30 days after 3 January 2016` r
    AND NOT r's `at least one authorised representative was appointed within 30 days after 3 January 2016`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 45(8)"
GIVEN `an application for registration under the repealed Act was pending immediately before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pending application is treated as an application under the corresponding provisions of this Act` IF
    `an application for registration under the repealed Act was pending immediately before 3 January 2016`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 45(9)"
GIVEN t IS A `Transitional Registration Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reservation is treated as a reservation under this Act` IF
    t's `a reservation of name under section 13(3) of the repealed Act had not expired before 3 January 2016`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 45(9)"
GIVEN t IS A `Transitional Registration Facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the date the transitional reservation expires` MEANS
    t's `the date the reservation would have expired if the repealed Act were still in force`

-- 45(6) and (7) (a prescribed person may keep using the old electronic service until a
-- Gazetted date, and that service is treated as the electronic transaction system), 45(10)
-- (a pending appeal is dealt with under the repealed Act), 45(11) (investigations, orders
-- and rights of appeal under the repealed Act are unaffected), 45(12) (old subsidiary
-- legislation continues), 45(13) (references to the repealed Act are read as references to
-- this Act) and 45(14) (definition of "repealed Act"): savings, continuations and a
-- definition with no condition a fact of a case can satisfy, inert.
